    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, our lineup leans heavily into efficiency, headlined by **Christian Yelich** (75.84) and **Yordan Alvarez** (74.97). **Yelich** is our premier play, benefiting from a high-upside matchup against Andrew Painter and a significant +13% platoon boost that maximizes his output in the leadoff spot. **Junior Caminero** (74.72) also warrants attention; despite the volatility of his profile, the favorable 5.47 xERA of Sam Aldegheri provides an elite ceiling for his power tools. We are also banking on **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (71.57) to capitalize on a +14% platoon adjustment, as his speed profile remains a vital anchor for our stolen base needs against Landen Roupp.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision involved **Colt Keith** (56.96), who just missed the cut. While **Keith** carries a respectable projection, he was nudged out by the specific efficiency gains of **Casey Schmitt** (63.92) and **Luke Raley** (62.96). **Schmitt** is positioned to feast on Javier Assad due to a +15% SP skill advantage and the massive situational boost of batting at the top of the order. Meanwhile, **Raley** draws a favorable park factor and a +19% matchup edge against the struggling Littell. We remain cautious regarding **Trea Turner** (50.39) and **Kyle Schwarber** (49.63); both are forced to contend with the elite arm of Jacob Misiorowski, whose 2.79 xERA effectively suppresses their overall score despite their consistent lineup placement.\n\nLooking ahead, nearly all of our starters are currently flagged as \"Lineup Pending.\" While our projections assume standard order placement, users should monitor the confirmed cards, as a dip for **Dillon Dingler** or **Gary Sanchez** could force a pivot to the bench. Furthermore, while the wind is providing a slight tailwind for **Carson Benge** (60.24) against Spencer Strider, the difficulty of the matchup dictates a \"start and monitor\" approach rather than high-confidence anchoring. Our goal today is to leverage these specific platoon edges to stay competitive in the AVG and SB categories, keeping a close watch on **Yelich** and **Crow-Armstrong** to provide the necessary spark.",
